<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — auto-closing timed "toast" message popup (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms Forms/FormTimedMessage
    (FormTimedMessage.cs + FormTimedMessage.Designer.cs), per AAP §0.3.3 — never a redesign.
    It shows a bold title plus a message, is pinned near the top-left of the screen by the
    code-behind, and auto-closes after a caller-supplied timeout.

    Pairs with the code-behind FormTimedMessageView.axaml.cs via
    x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormTimedMessageView" (namespace AgOpenGPS.Views). That code-behind
    assigns lblMessage.Text / lblMessage2.Text, pins the window position (Left=20, Top=20) and runs
    the one-shot auto-close timer (WinForms System.Windows.Forms.Timer -> Avalonia DispatcherTimer);
    the x:Name values below are that contract. This view sets NO DataContext and uses NO {Binding},
    so no x:DataType is declared — the text is supplied imperatively, exactly like the original
    WinForms ctor FormTimedMessage(int timeInMsec, string titleString, string messageString).

    Window attribute provenance (WinForms FormTimedMessage.Designer.cs / .cs):
      Title="AgOpenGPS Message"        maps to  this.Text = "AgOpenGPS Message"
      SystemDecorations="None"         maps to  this.FormBorderStyle = None (+ ControlBox = false)
      Topmost="True"                   maps to  this.TopMost = true
      ShowInTaskbar="False"            maps to  this.ShowInTaskbar = false
      CanResize="False"                maps to  borderless, fixed popup (no resize grips)
      SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"   maps to  ctor computed ClientSize from label PreferredSize
      WindowStartupLocation="Manual"   maps to  this.StartPosition = Manual (Left/Top set in code-behind)
      Background="Red"                 maps to  this.BackColor = Color.Red
      Padding="7"                      maps to  this.Padding = new Padding(7)  (the red border thickness)

    Inner surface (WinForms panel1: Dock=Fill, BackColor=OldLace):
      The OldLace Border fills the area inside the 7px Window padding, so the Red Window background
      shows through as a 7px frame around the OldLace panel — visually identical to the original.

    Labels (WinForms lblMessage / lblMessage2 — both Tahoma 18, autosize):
      lblMessage  (title)   : Tahoma 18 Bold,    designer Location (3, 0)   -> Margin "3,0,0,0".
      lblMessage2 (message) : Tahoma 18 regular, designer Location (43, 52) -> Margin "43,23,0,0".
                              In a vertical StackPanel both labels share the same left origin (the
                              Border's inner-left), so the left value 43 reproduces the WinForms
                              absolute Location.X = 43 directly. The top value 23 is the WinForms
                              inter-label gap (message Top 52 minus the ~29px Tahoma-18-Bold title
                              height), applied as the StackPanel top margin so the message sits the
                              same distance below the title. The Border Padding reproduces the
                              original's roomy ClientSize (ctor added +60 width / +30 height) so
                              SizeToContent yields the same padded look.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormTimedMessageView"
        Title="AgOpenGPS Message"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        CanResize="False"
        SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"
        WindowStartupLocation="Manual"
        Background="Red"
        Padding="7">

    <!-- WinForms panel1: Dock=Fill, BackColor=OldLace. Sits inside the 7px red Window padding,
         so the Red Window Background frames it on every side. -->
    <Border Background="OldLace"
            Padding="16,12">

        <!-- Vertical stack mirrors the two stacked WinForms labels. -->
        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical">

            <!-- WinForms lblMessage (title): Tahoma 18 Bold @ (3, 0). Text set at runtime by the
                 code-behind; "Message" is the original designer placeholder. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblMessage"
                       Margin="3,0,0,0"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="18"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Text="Message" />

            <!-- WinForms lblMessage2 (message): Tahoma 18 regular @ (43, 52). In a StackPanel the
                 siblings share one left origin, so left=43 matches the WinForms absolute X exactly;
                 top=23 is the WinForms inter-label gap. "Message 2" is the designer placeholder. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblMessage2"
                       Margin="43,23,0,0"
                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                       FontSize="18"
                       Text="Message 2" />

        </StackPanel>

    </Border>

</Window>
